        "In addition, the proposed Eastern Rajasthan Canal Project (ERCP) aims to harness surplus monsoon floodwaters of the Chambal, Kunnu, Kul, Parbati, Kalisindh, and Mej river basins to provide reliable drinking and irrigation water to thirteen eastern and south-eastern districts. Inter-basin water transfers, integrated river basin management, and continuous desiltation of feeder channels represent the cornerstone of Rajasthan long-term water security and agricultural resilience."
