        "Endowed with vast expanses of barren arid land, minimal cloud cover, and over three hundred twenty-five days of intense clear sunshine annually, Rajasthan has emerged as the undisputed leader of India solar and renewable energy revolution. With an estimated solar power potential exceeding one hundred forty-two gigawatts—the highest in the country—the state government enacted the visionary Rajasthan Solar Energy Policy, 2019, and the Rajasthan Wind and Hybrid Energy Policy to incentivize large-scale capital investments, build state-of-the-art solar parks, and facilitate green energy evacuation corridors connecting western desert powerhouses to the national power grid.",
