        "Beyond centralized utility-scale solar farms, Rajasthan has aggressively expanded rooftop solar installations under the PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojana and decentralized solar agricultural feeders under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Urja Suraksha evam Utthaan Mahabhiyan (PM-KUSUM) scheme. PM-KUSUM Component A and Component C enable farmers and village cooperatives to install grid-connected solar power plants on barren farmlands and solarize existing grid-connected agricultural tube wells. Farmers not only generate free daytime electricity for irrigation but also earn steady recurring revenue by feeding surplus green electricity back to state power distribution companies (DISCOMs) via net metering.",
        "In addition to solar energy, western Rajasthan possesses exceptional wind energy potential, particularly along the windy sand ridges of Jaisalmer, Barmer, and Pratapgarh. The state has actively pioneered hybrid renewable energy parks that co-locate wind turbines and solar photovoltaic arrays on the same land parcel. Hybrid plants optimize land utilization, share high-voltage electrical substation infrastructure, and provide balanced power output, as solar peak generation during bright sunny afternoons is complemented by high wind velocities during evening and night hours.",
