        "Community-driven wildlife protection is deeply rooted in Rajasthan cultural ethos, especially among the Bishnoi community. Bishnoi villages provide inviolable sanctuary to the State Animal (Chinkara or Indian Gazelle), Blackbucks, and the State Tree (Khejri). The Tal Chhapar Sanctuary in Churu district is famous for large herds of elegant Blackbucks, while the Kumbhalgarh and Mount Abu sanctuaries protect leopards, Indian wolves, and sloth bears in sub-tropical montane forests.",
