        "Providing universal, equitable, high-quality, and cashless healthcare coverage to all citizens is a cardinal commitment of public policy in Rajasthan. The state has emerged as a national pioneer in implementing comprehensive health assurance and insurance schemes designed to protect families from catastrophic out-of-pocket medical expenditures during illness and hospitalizations. By integrating central and state healthcare initiatives, including the Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) and the Mukhyamantri Ayushman Arogya Yojana (MAAY), the state ensures universal access to secondary and tertiary medical treatments.",
        "Under the Mukhyamantri Ayushman Arogya Yojana, eligible beneficiary families registered under the Jan Aadhaar ecosystem receive cashless indoor medical treatment benefits up to twenty-five lakh rupees per family per year across an extensive network of empanelled government and private hospitals. The scheme covers more than one thousand seven hundred clinical packages, including complex surgical procedures, cardiac surgeries, neurosurgery, organ transplants, cancer chemotherapy, joint replacements, and post-hospitalization medications, providing a comprehensive safety net for vulnerable citizens.",
        "To complement indoor hospitalization coverage, the state operates the Mukhyamantri Nishulk Dawa Yojana (Free Medicine Scheme) and Mukhyamantri Nishulk Jach Yojana (Free Diagnostic Tests Scheme) across all state-run healthcare facilities, ranging from Sub-Health Centres and Primary Health Centres (PHCs) to Community Health Centres (CHCs), Sub-District Hospitals, and apex Medical College Hospitals. Through these schemes, thousands of essential generic medicines, surgical sutures, and hundreds of pathology and radiology diagnostic tests (including blood biochemistry, X-rays, USG, CT scans, and MRI) are provided entirely free of cost to all walk-in outdoor and indoor patients.",
